# The canon itself is meant to be committed — `acts.jsonl` is this
# repository's own rules and CONTRIBUTING.md links into them. These are not:
#
#   seen         this machine's ingest state. Committed, it conflicts on
#                every pull and tells everyone which candidates one person
#                personally declined.
#   draft-runs/  the evidence from this machine's model runs.
#   config       the endpoint and model name on ONE machine. `canon draft`
#                on a fresh clone should say "no endpoint configured", not
#                fail against a port on somebody else's laptop.
#
# `secrets/` is not listed because it writes its own `.gitignore` of `*` the
# first time a lot is sealed — a sealed secret that travels with the
# repository has been published to everyone who clones it.
seen
draft-runs/
config
